{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-phi-q-piece","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:phi-q-piece","kind":"definition","title":"Φ$_q$-piece sub-link $K_S$ of a braid closure","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-bloch-group"],"cites":["references/kauffman1991","references/faddeev1994"],"tags":["phi-q","kashaev","smoothing","skein","sub-link","archimedean"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.PhiQPiece.subLink","text":"phi-q-piece.md","leanSource":"phi-q-piece.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"def:phi-q-piece\"></a><p>Let <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\beta \\in B_n</code> be a braid. For each subset <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S \\subseteq \\{0, \\dots, n-2\\}</code>, the <strong><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\Phi_q</code>-piece <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K_S \\subseteq S^3</code></strong> is the link obtained from <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\widehat{\\beta}</code> by <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">L_0</code>-smoothing every crossing not in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code> while leaving crossings in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">S</code> intact.</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-piece.md","heading":"Definition","number":"13.15.5","page":"b/def-phi-q-piece","qa":{"counts":{"pass":78,"fail":2,"warn":1,"na":11,"unknown":0,"stale":66},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:MathlibExt.PhiQPiece.subLink","via":"sibling","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/phi-q-piece.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
